BBUUGGSS
     The aaccll__ffrroomm__tteexxtt() and aaccll__ttoo__tteexxtt() functions rely on the getpwent(3)
     library calls to manage username and uid mapping, as well as the
     getgrent(3) library calls to manage groupname and gid mapping.  These
     calls are not thread safe, and so transitively, neither are
     aaccll__ffrroomm__tteexxtt() and aaccll__ttoo__tteexxtt().  These functions may also interfere
     with stateful calls associated with the ggeettppwweenntt() and ggeettggrreenntt() calls.

